            <ArticleTitle>Surgical Stabilization of Rib Fractures in a 6-Year-Old Child After Blunt Trauma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e439-e441</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0003-4975(17)31074-3</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.athoracsur.2017.07.034</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>When identified, rib fractures in children are associated with high-energy trauma, nonaccidental trauma, or both. Traditionally, the optimal management of rib fractures in children is supportive care. In this case report, we present a 6-year-old boy who underwent surgical rib fixation for multiple displaced and comminuted rib fractures after being stepped on by a horse.</AbstractText>
